{{also|Dinsdag}}
==Dutch==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|nl|dum|dinsendach}}. Probably from {{der|nl|gem-pro|*þingsus-dagaz|t=Day of Thingsus}}, from {{m|gem-pro|*þingsus}} + {{m|gem-pro|*dagaz}}. {{m|la|Thingsus}}, {{m|ang|Tiw}} or {{m|non|Týr}} was the name of the {{der|nl|gem|-}} god of justice.

Compare Low German {{m|nds-de|Dingsdag}} and German {{m|de|Dienstag}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|nl|/ˈdɪns.dɑx/}}
* {{audio|nl|Nl-dinsdag.ogg}}
* {{hyphenation|nl|dins|dag}}

===Noun===
{{nl-noun|m|-:en|+}}

# [[Tuesday]]
#: {{uxi|nl|We hebben op '''dinsdag''' een vergadering.|We have a meeting on '''Tuesday'''.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|De '''dinsdagen''' zijn altijd mijn langste dagen op werk.|The '''Tuesdays''' are always my longest workdays.}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Het was een rustig '''dinsdagje''' voor me.|It was a quiet '''Tuesday''' for me.}}

